<title>ESTONIA: HANSA INSURANCE APPROVES LAST YEAR RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HANSA INSURANCE APPROVES LAST YEAR RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonian insurance company Hansa Kindlustus, a subsidiary of Swedish Trygg-Hansa, on Wednesday approved its financial results for 1996, which showed a net profit of 1.8 million kroons.</p>
<p>Hansa Kindlustus collected premiums of 23.5 million kroons and made payments worth 1.46 million kroons last year, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company is also active in the Latvian and Lithuanian non-life insurance markets.</p>
<p>The board also decided to change the company's strategy to be aggressive to increase its market share, the company added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
